Here’s a minimal, self‑contained **React Todo List** component that lets you:

* **Add** new items
* **Toggle** an item between completed / not completed
* **Delete** items

You can drop the code straight into a React project (e.g. a Create‑React‑App `src/App.js`) and it will work out‑of‑the‑box.

```jsx
import React, { useState } from "react";
import "./TodoList.css";   // optional – see CSS below

function TodoList() {
  // The list of todos – each todo is { id, text, completed }
  const [todos, setTodos] = useState([]);

  // Current value of the “new todo” input field
  const [newText, setNewText] = useState("");

  // Add a new todo
  const handleAdd = (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    const trimmed = newText.trim();
    if (!trimmed) return;

    setTodos((prev) => [
      ...prev,
      {
        id: Date.now(),           // simple unique id
        text: trimmed,
        completed: false,
      },
    ]);
    setNewText("");
  };

  // Toggle completed flag
  const toggleComplete = (id) => {
    setTodos((prev) =>
      prev.map((t) =>
        t.id === id ? { ...t, completed: !t.completed } : t
      )
    );
  };

  // Delete a todo
  const handleDelete = (id) => {
    setTodos((prev) => prev.filter((t) => t.id !== id));
  };

  return (
    <div className="todo-container">
      <h2>Todo List</h2>

      {/* Form to add a new todo */}
      <form onSubmit={handleAdd} className="todo-form">
        <input
          type="text"
          placeholder="What needs to be done?"
          value={newText}
          onChange={(e) => setNewText(e.target.value)}
        />
        <button type="submit">Add</button>
      </form>

      {/* List of todos */}
      <ul className="todo-list">
        {todos.map((todo) => (
          <li key={todo.id} className={todo.completed ? "completed" : ""}>
            <span
              onClick={() => toggleComplete(todo.id)}
              className="todo-text"
            >
              {todo.text}
            </span>

            <button
              onClick={() => handleDelete(todo.id)}
              className="delete-btn"
              aria-label="Delete"
            >
              ✕
            </button>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  );
}

export default TodoList;
```

---

### Optional CSS (`TodoList.css`)

```css
.todo-container {
  max-width: 400px;
  margin: 2rem auto;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
}

.todo-form {
  display: flex;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}

.todo-form input {
  flex: 1;
  padding: 0.5rem;
  font-size: 1rem;
}

.todo-form button {
  padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
  font-size: 1rem;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.todo-list {
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 0;
}

.todo-list li {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #e0e0e0;
}

.todo-list li.completed .todo-text {
  text-decoration: line-through;
  color: #777;
}

.todo-text {
  flex: 1;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.delete-btn {
  background: transparent;
  border: none;
  color: #c00;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  cursor: pointer;
}
```

---

#### How to use it

```jsx
// src/App.js
import React from "react";
import TodoList from "./TodoList";

function App() {
  return (
    <div>
      <TodoList />
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
```

That’s it—no external libraries are required beyond React itself. Feel free to extend the component (e.g., add persistence with `localStorage`, filter views, edit items, etc.) as your project grows. Enjoy building!
